codex
The repo confirms both security gaps: `write_file` lacks the shell sandbox’s executable-config deny list, and OpenAPI connections have no app permission gate. I also found that eve recall doesn’t remove omitted records, so a bounded memory design needs to replace one aggregate record to prevent stale notes from accumulating.

